      'Sixteen girls then laid their bicycles down in front of the wheels.',
      'He got away. Bicycles do not stop a truck. But by then the girls had the one thing that mattered more than the roadblock: they knew the number. They called CHILDLINE 1098, and what they said set a search running that pulled in the local police and the border force. The driver abandoned the child in a settlement nearby and was picked up later. The boy got home.',
      'The change had already happened before any of that, though, in the few seconds on the road. A group of adolescent girls had looked at a situation that was not theirs, decided it was theirs, refused the first explanation an adult gave them, and used a system they had been taught to trust. That is not bravery arriving from nowhere. That is what a rights education looks like when it is finally needed.',
