      'Within about six months he was conducting the meetings himself.',
      'The Child Parliament gave him something to be confident about, which is the part that is easy to miss. He was not learning public speaking in the abstract. He was learning to speak about school, health, protection, and children\u2019s right to a childhood \u2014 real questions with real answers owed. Confidence built on top of something worth saying tends to stay.',
      'It leaves a question worth asking of every parliament: who gets nominated, who gets elected, who actually gets heard. A child cabinet can reproduce the hierarchies of the village it sits in, or it can be the first place a child from an excluded household is listened to.',
