    line: '2010\u201313 \u00b7 Jamunaha, Shravasti \u00b7 School of Leadership',
    lead: 'An order can interrupt an event. It cannot change the thing that produced the event.',
    body: [
      'In 2010\u201311 word came that a twelve-year-old girl was to be married. The police were brought in. The Sub-Divisional Magistrate was engaged. The ceremony was stopped.',
      'Three days later the organisation learned that the marriage had taken place at another location.',
      'That is the whole of the failure and there is no softening it. Every part of the enforcement route worked exactly as designed, and a twelve-year-old was married anyway, because the family had simply moved the event beyond the reach of the order.',
      'What follows is the reason this story is told at all. The conclusion drawn was not that enforcement should be applied harder. It was that an order changes an afternoon, and the beliefs, relationships and pressures that arranged the wedding were all still standing the following morning.',
      'So the work moved inside the village. Every learning centre was tied to a parents\u2019 committee, and those committees began meeting monthly to talk about what early marriage and interrupted education actually cost. Locally recruited women educators kept their relationships with the girls and with the households at the same time, so that when a marriage began being discussed there was a chance of hearing about it early, and a person the family already knew who could go and sit with them.',
      'Parents were not treated as an enemy to be beaten. They were asked to think about their daughter\u2019s health, her schooling, and what her choices would look like at twenty. When one family would not move, other parents in the committee were in the room to say something.',
      'The programme records 26 marriages stopped. It also ran a survey of 114 families to understand why early marriage was happening at all, and let what came back reshape the response.',
      'An organisation that hides its failed cases learns nothing from them. This one wrote its worst outcome into the record and changed its method because of it.',
    ],
