    title: 'Almost every girl here stopped at Class VIII. Twenty of them got on the road to Bahraich',
    dek: 'The cliff is not literacy. It is the year a girl turns fourteen and the nearest school gets too far away.',
    line: '2016\u201317 \u00b7 Fourteen villages and Bahraich \u00b7 School of Leadership',
    lead: 'Reading and writing were common in these villages. Finishing school was almost unheard of.',
    body: [
      'A survey across fourteen villages found a dropout rate of 96.7 per cent among girls after Class VIII. Basic literacy was widespread. Secondary completion had all but vanished.',
      'The two facts together tell you where the barrier sits. It is not that these families do not value education, and it is not that the girls cannot learn. It is that at a certain age the nearest school stops being in the village, and everything that follows \u2014 the distance, the cost, the road, what people will say about a girl travelling \u2014 becomes a family decision rather than an academic one.',
      'Bravo Girls put academic support, leadership learning, rights and health education around the girls, and kept talking to the households. The teachers were women, trained, and from nearby, so the girls could see the thing they were being asked to imagine.',
      'Twenty of thirty participants travelled from forest villages into Bahraich and enrolled in Class XI. Twenty-six went on from Class XI into Class XII. Twenty-six completed matriculation.',
      'The travelling is not a footnote to this story. It is the story. Every one of those girls is making a journey her mother did not make, on roads her family worried about, to sit in a classroom in a city where she does not live.',
      'And the families changed their minds, which was the harder shift. Mothers and younger siblings were affected by watching it happen, and that is how a 96.7 per cent dropout rate eventually moves \u2014 not because anyone is persuaded in the abstract, but because a girl from four houses down is now in Class XII.',
    ],
    pull: 'Every one of those girls is making a journey her mother did not make.',
    actTitle: 'The gap is transport, hostel and fees',
    act: 'These girls did not need convincing and neither did their families in the end. What stood in the way was the cost of getting to a city classroom and staying there.',
    actCta: 'Invest in a girl\u2019s transition year',
