    title: 'The women holding up maternal health were waiting months for their own payments',
    dek: 'An ASHA is the last mile of the public health system. Her working conditions are a health issue, not an HR one.',
    line: '2007\u201308 \u00b7 Payagpur and Chittaura, Bahraich \u00b7 Rights & Entitlements',
    lead: 'A newborn in a forest village meets the health system through one woman who lives nearby.',
    body: [
      'ASHAs connect pregnant women, newborns and families to public health services. Six orientations reached 147 of them across the two blocks. The content was clinical and practical: recognising danger signs in mothers and newborns, keeping village health records, cord and thermal care, what a postpartum home visit should cover.',
      'Alongside them ran orientations for village heads, block officials and Rogi Kalyan Samiti members \u2014 deliberately, because technical training that lands in a workforce nobody supports does not survive contact with the month.',
      'Which is how the payment issue surfaced. ASHAs are paid incentives against tasks, and those payments were not arriving regularly. In the meetings, that stopped being described as a private inconvenience for individual women and started being described as what it is: something the public system that depends on them could put right.',
      'The work then followed the ordinary route. The issue was raised with the block officials responsible. Written applications went to higher authorities where the block could not resolve it. The same interfaces took up staffing, birth registration, referral arrangements and the use of village health funds.',
      'Whether every rupee was released is not what changed here. What changed is that a workforce accustomed to receiving instructions acquired a channel of its own — a forum, with officials in it who had the power to act, where the women’s working conditions could be raised as business rather than as complaint.',
      'That reframing is the change. The person closest to the community is strengthened, a forum is built around her, and the forum is connected to institutions that can do something. Care at the last mile is only as reliable as the terms on which the last mile works.',
    ],
