    title: 'He risked two biswa on a local variety, and decided it was worth more',
    dek: 'For a smallholder, an experiment that fails is not a data point. It is a season. So he made the experiment small.',
    line: 'November 2024\u2013April 2025 \u00b7 Sirsiyanpurwa, Bahraich \u00b7 Climate Justice',
    lead: 'Trying something new is a luxury priced in months of food.',
    body: [
      'Radheshyam, a member of Ganga Aajeevika Adhikar Sangathan, bounded his risk deliberately: a two-biswa onion plot, variety recorded as \u201cJirat,\u201d which he describes as local or desi.',
      'Nursery on 1 November 2024, transplanted 26 December, harvested 28 April 2025 after 127 days. Two quintals and ten kilograms.',
      'Almost everything came from the household. His own land, his own land preparation and labour, cow dung as the fertility input. Seed was facilitated through the programme. The only cash cost in the form is \u20b9150 for irrigation.',
      'Gross income \u20b93,150, net \u20b93,000. Read that as cash flow, not profitability: own labour, land and manure carry no monetary value in the record.',
      'His conclusion is the actual outcome. He considered the production good, described the crop as fully organic, and intends to grow more next season. The change here is not \u20b93,000. It is a farmer holding evidence about a specific variety on his own soil and deciding what to do with it.',
      'The AAS is where a private trial can become shared knowledge \u2014 if the discussion includes costs, labour and the attempts that did not work. That is the difference between farmers learning from each other and farmers being told.',
      'Local varieties and low-purchased-input methods reduce dependency, which matters more each year the weather is less predictable. One season is not proof. Prices move, pests arrive, and what works on two biswa may not repeat on twenty. He intends to plant it again, which is the only test that counts.',
    ],
