      'Her 2024\u201325 onion trial used three biswa. Nursery 25 October 2024, transplanting 5 December, lifting from 10 March: 136 days. Two and a half quintals. Receipts \u20b99,500, total cost \u20b93,500, net return \u20b96,000. Seed and land rent are recorded at zero; labour at \u20b91,800 is the largest line.',
      'The story is not the yield. Her own account connects the cultivation to confidence, to what the household eats and to buying less. Membership of a livelihood-rights collective put that farming inside a wider space where women compare results and raise entitlements and local concerns in the same meeting.',
      'One onion season cannot show whether the soil improved or whether the returns hold. What it does support is narrower: she diversified into vegetables and spices, completed a documented trial, and built skills that outlast a single distribution of seed.',
