    dek: 'Arrears of \u20b925,000 to \u20b938,000 against households with irregular supply. Separately, each one is an argument nobody wins.',
    line: 'April 2026 onward \u00b7 Fakirpuri, Bahraich \u00b7 Rights & Entitlements',
    lead: 'A confusing bill is a private problem. Seventy confusing bills are a pattern.',
    body: [
      'Fakirpuri is a Tharu-majority village close to the India\u2013Nepal border. Families had received electricity connections intended for Scheduled Tribe households, and the supply that actually reached them stayed irregular and limited. Meanwhile the bills arriving bore little relationship to what anyone was using.',
      'The amounts were not small. Arrears of roughly \u20b925,000 to \u20b938,000 were shown against individual households. Some families had paid in part and watched the outstanding figure keep rising. For households on limited and uncertain income, that is not an administrative error. It is the fear of disconnection attached to a debt nobody can explain.',
      'Fakirpuri\u2019s Aajeevika Adhikar Sangathan brings together one earning member from each participating household, and its monthly meetings are where livelihood concerns and service problems get said out loud. In April 2026, women and other members brought their electricity bills into the same conversation.',
      'Comparing them changed what the problem was. What each family had understood as a confusing personal liability turned out to be a pattern: unusually high arrears across several households despite limited supply, and payments that were not showing up where residents expected. The group decided a collective, evidence-based approach would carry more weight than a series of separate complaints.',
      'Community coordinator Saman Kausar helped organise it. Working with the affected families she prepared a list of households and encouraged members, particularly women, to present their concerns together. Families gathered old payment receipts and consumption information. That let the community move past a general assertion of unfairness and put specific discrepancies on the table.',
      'She contacted the electricity department\u2019s junior engineer and explained the scale of it. Rather than sending families to the department one at a time, the organisation invited departmental representatives to the village. Residents put their receipts, their bills and their account of the actual supply in front of the officials.',
      'The department reviewed the evidence and cancelled approximately \u20b96 lakh in erroneous billing across about seventy families.',
      'The relief is the clearest result. The method is the durable one. Women who had identified and presented the problem saw that an administrative decision can be questioned through organised, documented engagement, and families now have a working example of receipts as instruments of accountability rather than paper in a tin.',
      'The supply is still limited. What changed is the disputed burden on these households, and a community that has proved it can bring a shared concern to the authority responsible for it.',
    ],
