    lead: 'Women who are never consulted about construction are the ones whose children sit under the roof.',
    body: [
      'The change started before the dispute. Women who had had little interaction outside their households formed a self-help group. Saving, borrowing and talking through shared difficulties gave them practice at acting together. Adult literacy learning added the rest: members who had treated illiteracy as a permanent limit began signing their names and handling public matters directly.',
      'That capacity mattered when someone noticed the roof of the new primary-school building leaking while construction was still underway. A defective roof is not a small inconvenience. Accepted, it would define the safety and quality of the space the village\u2019s children were expected to learn in for years.',
      'The women decided to stop the construction. They went to the site and told the contractor work should not continue unless good-quality material was used.',
      'They kept assembling whenever officials came to inspect, carrying brooms as the visible sign of what they were doing. It went on for four months.',
      'The contractor rebuilt the roof with better material.',
      'The protagonist here is the collective. One member narrated the episode, but the leverage came from members deciding together, staying present and refusing to let an unsafe public asset be signed off as though nothing was wrong.',
      'DEHAT\u2019s part came earlier: facilitating the group, the literacy learning and the discussion of rights. It did not find the leak or lead the protest.',
      'This widens what educational leadership means. Supporting a child\u2019s right to education is not only enrolment. It is asking whether the building is safe, whether public money produced a usable facility, and whether the women routinely left out of construction decisions can question the quality of local works.',
    ],
    pull: 'The result was concrete enough to stand beneath.',
    actTitle: 'Someone has to check the work',
    act: 'A savings group, literacy classes and rights discussion. None of it was about school buildings. All of it is why the roof got rebuilt.',
