    title: 'A helpline makes a crisis visible. It cannot keep a child safe through what follows',
    dek: 'Immediate response, medical care, shelter, documentation, a Committee decision, tracing, school re-entry, follow-up. Eight systems, one child.',
    line: '2016\u201317 \u00b7 Bahraich and the border networks \u00b7 Human Protection',
    lead: 'The number is the entry point. Everything that decides the outcome happens after the call ends.',
    body: [
      'The HR4 framework set out to connect the stages rather than treat them as separate interventions. A child may need immediate response, medical care, shelter, documentation, a Child Welfare Committee decision, family tracing, cross-border coordination, school re-entry and long-term follow-up \u2014 usually in that order and usually across different institutions.',
      'The community was the first part of the pathway, not an audience for it. Door-to-door campaigns and one-to-one contact helped families understand child rights, missing-child response and trafficking risk. Regular children\u2019s meetings gave children somewhere to raise a concern. Fifteen thousand people were reached through household campaigns, and 1,272 hours of individual community contact were recorded across the year.',
      'That is prevention and trust-building \u2014 the work through which a risk becomes visible before, or at the moment, a family contacts a formal service.',
      'When something urgent surfaced, CHILDLINE 1098 was the round-the-clock entry point. What happened next depended on the network: Child Welfare Committees, police, health and labour departments, railways, panchayats, civil-society organisations, and in border cases actors in Nepal and the security agencies. Case documentation and government child-tracking systems kept identity and responsibility attached to a child moving between institutions.',
      'The year recorded 377 children safely returned to their families and 88 children protected from sexual or other abuse and sent home after family counselling. Two children received a year of educational sponsorship. Those categories may overlap, and returned home is not the same as safely reintegrated.',
      'The change is the movement from an emergency number towards a continuity system. Awareness, children\u2019s participation, helpline response, institutional coordination and family restoration placed on one pathway.',
      'That architecture matters most in an open-border region, where a child can move beyond the sight of one village or one district within a day.',
      'The next standard of evidence has to go past counting returns \u2014 to sustained reintegration, education continuity and follow-up over time. This is the platform that makes asking for that reasonable.',
    ],
    pull: 'Returned home is not the same as safely reintegrated.',
