      'DEHAT facilitated the practical information: what the demand provision says, what the written format looks like, where it goes. Workers decided to apply and supplied their own job-card and household details.',
      'Three thousand eight hundred and seventy-nine job-card holders submitted written employment demands. The reported result was 18,322 person-days of work.',
      'A dated written demand creates a traceable relationship between a worker and the institution that owes them. An informal request creates nothing at all. That is the difference the campaign was built around.',
      'DEHAT enabled the capacity, the formats and the connections. Workers were the claimants. Gram Panchayats and programme authorities remained responsible for registering the demands, allocating the work and paying the wages.',
