      'Leadership here emerged inside the educational process rather than alongside it. A girl explaining a lesson, discussing a career with her family, or simply letting her younger siblings watch her persist — that is what changed the environment around education. It was carried by a network of girls, families, mentors and teachers, not by one exceptional individual.',
