      'In rural communities where household computers and paid courses were uncommon, the conditions for learning to use one were rarely available together. Access without time is a demonstration. Time without permission to experiment is a queue.',
      'The Digitify initiative placed shared Hole in the Wall learning stations in and around government schools, and supported computer-learning centres for older students. Younger learners explored curriculum-linked activities. Adolescents worked on internet basics, office applications and content relevant to further study or work.',
