      'It reaches a parent, a teacher, a community worker, a helpline, a neighbour the child has decided to trust. The first responsibility of whoever receives it is not to question the child. It is to listen without blame, deal with immediate safety, and connect the child to the authorities who have the power to act.',
      'From that point police, the Child Welfare Committee, health services, legal actors and safe accommodation each carry a distinct duty. The difficulty is never the list of duties. It is continuity.',
      'A family may fear stigma or retaliation more than it fears the perpetrator. Medical and legal processes require travel and repeated retelling. Schooling breaks. Somewhere in this a child needs an adult who can explain what happens next without promising an outcome nobody controls.',
      'What these five records show is a network learning to accompany rather than refer: community social workers supporting disclosure and documentation, statutory bodies making the protection decisions, health and justice institutions running their mandated processes, and follow-up that asks about safety and school rather than about the case file.',
      'DEHAT facilitates and accompanies. It does not investigate or adjudicate. These children are not evidence of a programme working; their privacy and their recovery outrank any organisation’s need to show a result.',
